        "release_time": "1778418333000",
        "title": null,
        "content": "\"Review of Value Accumulation Mechanisms Across 159 Protocols: Revenue Matters More Than Tokenomics\" (Author: Connor King; Translated & Compiled by TechFlow)  \nThis article analyzes six categories of token value accumulation mechanisms across 159 crypto protocols and finds that revenue scale matters more than the mechanism itself. Protocols with daily revenue exceeding $500,000 delivered an average return of +8% over the past year, whereas the lowest-revenue group posted -81%. Mechanisms such as buyback-and-burn, fee distribution, and the ve model have not consistently generated alpha\u2014performance in many categories was even driven solely by a few top-tier projects (e.g., Hyperliquid). In contrast, pure governance tokens, LRTs, and meme tokens\u2014lacking both revenue generation and value accrual\u2014performed worst overall. Read the full article:",
        "author": "wublockchain12",
        "author_description": null,
        "author_avatar_url": "https://static.sosovalue.com/2026/05/10/28c31317-dc3c-4358-bfba-a8cfa779c86a.jpg",
